C.1.0. {"problem": "The replaced commit is recorded only by record_deployment, after the deploy has run. The stated purpose is that whoever deploys sees what was running before. At the time of the human `deploy` decision, replaced_commit is empty, so the deployer cannot use it to decide. The Environment's current_commit would be known earlier, but nothing reads it.", "where": "SKILL.md, Delivery action record_deployment; glossary 'replaced commit'", "kind": "behaviour"}
C.1.1. {"problem": "record_deployment always sets replaced_commit = params.replaced, including when the deploy was refused (deployed false). A refused deploy changed nothing, so the request would show a 'replaced' commit that was never replaced. The glossary says it is the commit running 'before this delivery was deployed'. Also, an absent replaced overwrites any earlier value with nothing, and the spec does not distinguish 'nothing was running' from 'not supplied'.", "where": "SKILL.md, Delivery record_deployment effects; glossary 'replaced commit'", "kind": "behaviour"}
